{
  "message": "I can help you with your MMS issue. First, I need to verify your account for security purposes. Could you please provide either your phone number, customer ID, or your full name along with your date of birth?"
}

{
  "message": "Thank you for providing your information, John. To help resolve your MMS issue, I’ll need to run a few quick checks on your phone. Could you please let me know if you are able to send regular text messages (SMS) and use mobile data (such as browsing the web) without any issues? This will help me narrow down the cause."
}

{
  "message": "Thank you for the details. The next step is to check if your messaging app has the necessary permissions to send MMS, especially access to storage. Please grant storage permission to your messaging app. On your device, please run the following action: grant_app_permission(app_name=messaging, permission=storage). Let me know once this is done, and we’ll continue troubleshooting if needed."
}

{
  "message": "Great, thank you for granting the storage permission. Yes, please try sending an MMS message again now. If it still does not work, let me know and we can continue with further troubleshooting steps."
}

{
  "message": "I see that you have used 15.1GB of data this cycle, which is over your plan's 15GB data limit. When your data limit is exceeded, MMS messages may not go through because they require mobile data. You can add more data (up to 2GB) to your line for $2.00 per GB. Would you like to refuel your data now so you can send MMS messages?"
}

{
  "message": "Your line has been successfully refueled with 2.0 GB of additional data for $4.00. You should now be able to send MMS messages. Please try sending your MMS again. If you still experience issues, let me know and we can continue troubleshooting."
}

{
  "message": "I'm glad to hear that your MMS messages are now going through! If you have any other questions or need further assistance in the future, feel free to reach out. Have a great day!"
}

{
  "message": "I can help you with your MMS issue. First, I need to verify your identity to access your account and provide support. Could you please provide either your phone number, customer ID, or your full name along with your date of birth?"
}

{
  "message": "Thank you for providing your information, John. To help you with your MMS issue, I’ll need you to perform a few quick checks and actions on your phone. First, can you please check if your phone is currently connected to a 2G, 3G, 4G, or 5G network? If you see that it’s on 2G, please change your network mode to prefer 4G/5G. Let me know what you find, or if you need instructions on how to check or change this setting."
}

{
  "message": "Please set your phone's network mode preference to '4G/5G preferred'. This will allow your phone to connect to faster networks that support MMS. Once you've done this, let me know if you are able to send MMS messages, or if you need further assistance."
}

{
  "message": "Thank you for updating your network mode. The next step is to check if your phone's mobile data is enabled, as MMS requires mobile data to work. Please check your phone's settings or status bar to confirm that mobile data is turned ON. If it is already enabled and you still can't send MMS, let me know so we can proceed with further troubleshooting."
}

{
  "message": "Thank you for confirming that mobile data is enabled. The next step is to check if your phone's APN (Access Point Name) settings are correct, as incorrect APN settings can prevent MMS from working. Please check your APN settings and let me know if you see an MMSC URL listed. If you’re unsure how to check this, I can guide you through the process."
}

{
  "message": "Thank you for checking your APN settings and confirming the MMSC URL is present. The next step is to check if Wi-Fi Calling is enabled on your device, as this can sometimes interfere with MMS. Please check your phone's settings to see if Wi-Fi Calling is ON. If it is, please turn it OFF and then try sending an MMS again. Let me know if this resolves the issue or if you need further assistance."
}

{
  "message": "Thank you for confirming that Wi-Fi Calling is off. The next step is to check if your messaging app has the necessary permissions to send MMS. Please check your messaging app's permissions and ensure that both 'storage' and 'SMS' permissions are granted. If either permission is missing, please grant it and try sending an MMS again. Let me know if you need instructions on how to check or change app permissions."
}

{
  "message": "Thank you for your patience. Since your network, data, APN, Wi-Fi Calling, and app permissions are all set correctly, let's try resetting your APN settings to default, as sometimes a reset can resolve hidden configuration issues. After resetting, you will need to reboot your device for the changes to take effect. Would you like instructions on how to reset your APN settings and reboot your phone?"
}

{
  "message": "Great! Please follow these steps:

1. Reset your APN settings to default. This option is usually found in your phone's network or mobile data settings under 'Access Point Names' or 'APN'. Look for an option like 'Reset to default' or 'Reset settings'.
2. After resetting the APN, please reboot (restart) your phone.

Once your phone has restarted, try sending an MMS message again. Let me know if this resolves the issue or if you need further assistance."
}

{
  "message": "Thank you for trying those steps. Since we've checked your network, data, APN, Wi-Fi Calling, app permissions, and performed a reset and reboot, we've covered all standard troubleshooting steps for MMS issues. At this point, I recommend escalating your case to a human technical support agent who can investigate further. I will transfer you now. YOU ARE BEING TRANSFERRED TO A HUMAN AGENT. PLEASE HOLD ON."
}

{
  "message": "I'd be happy to help you with your signal issue. To get started, I need to verify your account. Could you please provide either your phone number, customer ID, or your full name along with your date of birth?"
}

{
  "message": "Thank you for providing your information, John. To help diagnose the 'No Service' issue, could you please check your phone's status bar and let me know what icons or messages you see there? This will help me determine the next steps."
}

{
  "message": "It looks like Airplane Mode is currently enabled on your phone, which will prevent you from getting any cellular signal. Please turn off Airplane Mode on your device. Once you've done that, let me know if your signal returns or if you still see 'No Service.'"
}

{
  "message": "Thank you for the update. The next step is to check if your SIM card is being recognized by your phone. Please check your SIM card status on your device and let me know if it shows as active, missing, or locked."
}

{
  "message": "Since your phone isn't detecting the SIM card, please try removing the SIM card from your device and then reinserting it to ensure it's properly seated. After you've done this, let me know if your phone recognizes the SIM card or if the issue persists."
}

{
  "message": "Your line (555-123-2002) is currently suspended, which is why you have no service. This is due to an overdue bill on your account. I have just sent you a payment request for the overdue bill. Please check your payment requests and follow the instructions to complete the payment. Once the overdue bill is paid, I can help you restore your service."
}

{
  "message": "Your payment has been received and your line has been reactivated. Please reboot your phone now to restore your service. After restarting, you should see your signal return. If you still experience issues after rebooting, let me know and I’ll assist you further."
}

{
  "message": "Thank you for letting me know. Since your line is now active but your phone still shows 'No Signal,' let's check if your SIM card is being recognized after the restart. Please check your SIM card status again and let me know if it now shows as active, missing, or locked."
}

{
  "message": "YOU ARE BEING TRANSFERRED TO A HUMAN AGENT. PLEASE HOLD ON."
}

{
  "message": "I can definitely help you with your MMS (picture messaging) issue. First, I’ll need to verify your account for technical support. Could you please provide either your phone number, customer ID, or your full name along with your date of birth?"
}

{
  "message": "Thank you, John. I have located your account. To help you fix the MMS (picture messaging) issue, I’ll need to guide you through a few quick checks and steps on your phone. Are you able to follow instructions on your device right now?"
}

{
  "message": "No worries, I’ll guide you step by step and keep things simple. First, we need to make sure your messaging app has the right permissions to send picture messages. Please follow these instructions:

1. On your phone, please grant the SMS permission to your messaging app. This is usually found in your phone’s settings under Apps > Messaging > Permissions, then enable 'SMS'.

Let me know once you’ve done this, or if you need help finding the option."
}

{
  "message": "Yes, please go ahead and allow storage permission for your messaging app. This is necessary for sending and receiving picture messages (MMS). Once you’ve enabled storage permission, let me know, and we’ll continue with the next step."
}

{
  "message": "Thank you for updating the permissions. The next step is to check your SIM card connection, as issues with the SIM can also prevent MMS from working. Please follow these steps:

1. Remove your SIM card from your phone and then reinsert it securely. (If your phone has a SIM tray, use the SIM eject tool or a paperclip to open it.)
2. Once the SIM card is back in, wait for your phone to reconnect to the network.

Let me know when you’ve done this, or if you need help with any part of the process."
}

{
  "message": "Thank you for reseating your SIM card. I have also enabled data roaming on your line, which can help with sending picture messages, especially if you are outside your usual coverage area.\n\nPlease try sending a picture message (MMS) now. If it still doesn't work, let me know what happens or if you see any error messages. I'm here to help you until it's resolved!"
}

{
  "message": "I'm glad to hear that your picture messages are working again! There’s nothing else you need to do right now. If you ever have trouble sending MMS again, you can check that your messaging app has SMS and storage permissions, your SIM card is properly inserted, and data roaming is enabled if you’re outside your usual area.\n\nIf you have any other questions or need help in the future, feel free to reach out. Have a great day!"
}

{
  "message": "You're very welcome, John! I'm glad I could help, and I'm always here if you need assistance in the future. Have a wonderful day and enjoy sending your picture messages!"
}

{
  "message": "I can help you troubleshoot your MMS issue. First, I need to verify your account for technical support. Could you please provide either your phone number, customer ID, or your full name along with your date of birth?"
}

{
  "message": "Thank you for providing your information, John. To help resolve your MMS issue, I’ll need you to perform a few quick checks and actions on your phone. First, please check if Airplane Mode is turned OFF. If it is ON, please turn it OFF. You can do this by toggling Airplane Mode in your phone’s settings or quick menu. Let me know once you’ve done this, or if Airplane Mode was already OFF."
}

{
  "message": "Yes, please go ahead and turn Airplane Mode OFF. This will re-enable your phone's wireless connections, which are necessary for sending MMS messages. Let me know once you have turned it OFF."
}

{
  "message": "Great! Next, let's make sure your phone is set to use the best available network for MMS. Please set your network mode preference to '4G/5G Preferred' in your phone's settings. This will help ensure your phone can send and receive MMS messages. Let me know once you've done this."
}

{
  "message": "Thank you! Now, let's make sure your messaging app has the necessary permissions to send and receive MMS. Please grant the 'storage' permission to your messaging app in your phone's app settings. This allows the app to access and send media files. Let me know once you've granted this permission."
}

{
  "message": "Great! Next, let's make sure your mobile data is turned ON, as MMS requires an active data connection. Please go to your phone's settings and turn ON mobile data if it is currently OFF. Let me know once you've done this."
}

{
  "message": "Thank you! If you are currently outside your home network or traveling, please also make sure that data roaming is enabled on your phone. If you are not traveling or outside your usual coverage area, you can skip this step. Let me know if you need instructions on how to enable data roaming or if you are ready to test sending an MMS message now."
}

{
  "message": "Yes, please try sending an MMS message now. If it goes through successfully, your issue should be resolved. If you still experience problems, let me know and we can continue troubleshooting."
}

{
  "message": "I'm glad to hear that your MMS messages are working again! If you have any other questions or need further assistance in the future, feel free to reach out. Have a great day!"
}
